<title>HONG KONG: China OKs Shangri-La unit to list abroad.</title>
<headline>China OKs Shangri-La unit to list abroad.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asian hotel owner Shangri-La Asia Ltd said on Thursday that China's securities regulator last month approved the company's 50-percent-owned China World Trade Center Ltd request to seek an overseas listing.</p>
<p>&quot;The CSRC (China Securities Regulatory Commission) has apparently given its approval to China World Trade Center Ltd to seek a listing on overseas stock exchange,&quot; Shangri-La managing director Paul Bush said in an interview.</p>
<p>But the listing details, including which exchange will be targeted, had yet to be finalised, he said.</p>
<p>-- Carrie Lee (852) 2843 6590</p>
